801.41;+2500,;15~HF.STAGE III
801.41;+2500,;25~WP-start~9
Stage 3\\
Full-thickness loss of skin in which adipose (fat) is visible in the 
ulcer and granulation tissue and epibole (rolled wound edges) are often 
present. Slough and/or eschar may be visible. The depth of tissue damage 
varies by anatomical location; areas of significant adiposity can develop 
deep wounds. Undermining and tunneling may occur. Fascia, muscle, 
tendon, ligament, cartilage and/or bone are not exposed. If slough or 
eschar obscures the extent of tissue loss this is an Unstageable Pressure 
Injury.
801.41;+2500,;35~WP-start~2
