801.41;+2482,;25~WP-start~8
Pressure Ulcer/Injury\\
A pressure injury is localized damage to the skin and underlying soft 
tissue usually over a bony prominence or related to a medical or other 
device. The injury can present as intact skin or an open ulcer and may be 
painful. The injury occurs as a result of intense and/or prolonged 
pressure or pressure in combination with shear. The tolerance of soft 
tissue for pressure and shear may also be affected by microclimate, 
nutrition, perfusion, co-morbidities and condition of the soft tissue.
